 "kind": "statement",
 "title": "Cohomology-sheaf form of the direct-image theorem",
 "statement": "If $f:X_0\\to Y_0$ is separated and of finite type and a Weil sheaf\n$\\mathcal F$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w$, then\n$R^if_!\\mathcal F$ is $\\iota$-mixed of weights at most $w+i$ for\nevery $i$.",
 "source": {
  "document": "literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-deligne-laumon-general/sk-thm-dl-general-sheaf/cor-zl-rfshriek-sheaf.md",
  "place": "node cor-zl-rfshriek-sheaf, order 2849"
 },
 "stmt_deps": [
  "def-weil-pbc-qbar-category",
  "def-weil-pbc-scheme-conventions"
 ],
 "proof": [
  {
   "text": "Regard $\\mathcal F$ as a complex concentrated in degree zero. The\ndefinition [def-weil-complex-weights] identifies its upper bound\nwith membership in $D_{\\le w}$. Noetherian induction and the localization rule\n[lem-zl-open-closed-weight], in its morphism-level form\n[lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction] (source strata, target strata\nand coefficient filtrations), reduce to the source and target strata\nof [thm-zl-relative-noether]. The finite first arrow\n$\\nu$ preserves the upper weight bound by\n[lem-zl-finite-pushforward]; every subsequent affine-line\nprojection preserves it by [thm-zl-relative-line-step]. Repeated\nuse of the composition isomorphism [lem-zl-shriek-composition],\nin the form of the inheritance of the weight bound under composition\n[lem-zl-composition-weight-bound] (stated for sheaves; for a sheaf in\ndegree zero the bound $R^if_!\\mathcal F$ of weights at most $w+i$ is\nthe same as $Rf_!\\mathcal F\\in D_{\\le w}$ by\n[def-weil-complex-weights], so the complex-level steps supply its\nhypotheses),\ngives the bound for the whole factorization. The same localization\ninduction glues all strata, so $Rf_!\\mathcal F\\in D_{\\le w}(Y_0)$;\nreading the $i$th cohomology\nsheaf gives the asserted bound $w+i$ (in the punctual sense of\n[def-weil-punctual-weights]).",
   "uses": [
    "def-weil-complex-weights",
    "lem-zl-open-closed-weight",
    "lem-zl-morphism-open-closed-reduction",
    "thm-zl-relative-noether",
    "lem-zl-finite-pushforward",
    "thm-zl-relative-line-step",
    "lem-zl-shriek-composition",
    "lem-zl-composition-weight-bound",
    "def-weil-punctual-weights"
   ],
   "elementary": false
  }
 ],
